From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] [Layout] Run the atomics and read-modify-writes of a
 replicated loop once

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Upstream-pr: https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang/pull/3873

Rationale: When a T.Parallel loop has fewer iterations than the CTA thread count and writes a register fragment (store_fragment_buffers non-empty), layout inference replicates the loop across thread groups so every replica populates its fragment copy. Any shared or global atomic or read-modify-write inside the same loop was previously executed by every replica, multiplying updates by the replication factor. Guard shared/global non-idempotent writes inside replicated loops to run on replica 0 only, and reject replicated loops where a fragment value depends on a shared/global buffer modified in the same barrier-free segment.

Quality: Eliminates silent multi-replica atomic/RMW corruption in replicated T.Parallel loops while keeping all 33 existing spark-ds41f:1107 kernels byte-for-byte unchanged.

Tests: testing/python/layout/test_tilelang_ReplicatedParallelWritesOnce.py across two GPU boots on SM121.

Upstream-status: Backported from open upstream PR tile-ai/tilelang#3873 (fixes #3870).
